---
import Adr from "../../components/Adr.astro";
import Excerpt from "../../components/Excerpt.astro";
import Layer from "../../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import PageLink from "../../components/PageLink.astro";
import Path from "../../components/Path.astro";
import Rule from "../../components/Rule.astro";

const DEV = "deploy/dev";

const H = {
  short: "Iki on Kubernetes on a laptop, and in CI",
  how: "kind, Tilt and the production chart",
  rules: "What's pinned, what's faked, and the restore test",
  ref: "Targets and decisions",
};
const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: H.short },
  { id: "how", label: H.how },
  { id: "rules", label: H.rules },
  { id: "ref", label: H.ref },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title={H.short}>
    <p>
      Iki runs on Kubernetes everywhere, a laptop included: a kind cluster driven by Tilt, deployed
      with the same Helm chart as production. kindnet enforces the chart's network policies, so
      they're exercised locally. Tilt builds the server and worker images as a deployment does,
      with the plugins it pins. CI brings the same cluster up headless on every code change, runs
      the end-to-end checks, then backs the database up, restores it into a new one and checks the
      restore (<Adr n={[14, 22, 99]} />).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title={H.how}>
    <p>
      <code>make dev-up</code> creates the cluster (or reuses it) and starts Tilt; <Path
        p={`${DEV}/up.sh`}
      /> installs what Tilt doesn't manage: the CloudNativePG operator, the CSI snapshot driver and
      generated development secrets. The cluster's single node is pinned by digest, and its
      networking is kindnet:
    </p>
    <Excerpt file={`${DEV}/kind-config.yaml`} />
    <p>
      Tilt rebuilds the server image whenever code under <code>server/</code> changes. It builds it
      as a deployment does: the server image, then the plugins in <Path
        p={`${DEV}/plugins.lock.yaml`}
      />, built with <code>iki deploy build --allow-local</code> and added by <Path
        p="deploy/plugins.Dockerfile"
      />; the worker image the same way, with the plugins' environments built in (<Path
        p="Tiltfile"
      />, <Path p={`${DEV}/values-dev.yaml`} />). How a deployment's images are built is on <PageLink
        to="Releases and images"
      />.
    </p>
    <p>
      Beside Iki it runs what a deployment would have outside it, small: Postgres through
      CloudNativePG, SeaweedFS for object storage, Keycloak as the identity provider over OIDC and
      SAML, Mailpit for email, an OpenTelemetry collector with Grafana, a webhook receiver, a shared
      file system, and fake LIMS and FoldCloud APIs for the example plugins that call them (<Path
        p={`${DEV}/manifests`}
      />).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={4} title={H.rules}>
    <div class="rules">
      <Rule title="In CI, on every code change" open>
        <p>
          CI's dev-cluster job creates the kind cluster from the same config, then runs <code
            >make dev-ci</code
          >: <code>up.sh</code>, <code>tilt ci</code>, the end-to-end checks and the restore test
          (<Path p="Makefile" sym="dev-ci:" />, <Path p={`${DEV}/e2e.sh`} />). The job is part of
          "CI passed" (<PageLink to="Gates and CI" />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="The restore test">
        <p>
          It backs the dev database up, restores it into a new database, and checks the restore
          with <code>iki-server check_restore</code> against the same files bucket and keys: the
          restore must hold everything the live database held when the backup began, and every file
          its records name must be in storage. It drops the restored database when it's done (<Adr
            n="0099"
          />, <Path p={`${DEV}/restore-test.sh`} />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Pinned and local">
        <p>
          The CloudNativePG operator's chart is pinned by version and OCI digest, and Helm refuses it
          if the digest doesn't match. The builds' Wasm modules are built in Docker as the server
          image's are, so the cluster needs no Rust on the machine (<Path p={`${DEV}/build-wasm.sh`} />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Where the ADR and the code differ">
        <ul>
          <li>
            <Adr n="0099" /> says the restore test runs on every change; the dev-cluster job is skipped
            for docs-only changes.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Rule>
    </div>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title={H.ref}>
    <div class="refs">
      <h3>Targets</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><code>make dev-up</code>, <code>dev-down</code>, <code>dev-creds</code>, <code>dev-sso</code></li>
        <li><code>make dev-e2e</code>, <code>dev-restore-test</code>, <code>dev-ci</code></li>
        <li><code>make web-dev</code>: the web app with instant reloads, against the dev cluster</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Where</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Path p={`${DEV}/README.md`} />: what runs, and how to sign in</li>
        <li><Path p={DEV} />: the scripts, manifests and values</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Decisions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Adr n="0014" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0022" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0099" title /></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
